data_fete
# Phase identity: idealized stoichiometric beta-FeTe framework, PbO-type P4/nmm.
# Provenance: Rodriguez et al., JACS 132, 10006--10008 (2010),
# doi:10.1021/ja104004t; COD 4102703 (CC0):
# https://www.crystallography.net/cod/4102703.cif
# IMPORTANT IDEALIZATION: the experimental parent is Fe1.095Te at 250(2) K.
# cxr-mc supports only fully occupied sites, so the source's 0.095-occupied
# interstitial Fe 2c orbit at (0.25,0.25,0.7811) is intentionally omitted.
# The retained fully occupied framework Fe 2b and Te 2c sites are expanded in P1.
# The catalog B_ang2=0.6 A^2 is a modeling placeholder, not source-derived.
# Limiting checks: V=a^2*c, Fe2Te2, finite basal (001) coupling.
# Validation: fete-p4nmm-idealized-structure
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
_cell_length_a 3.8139
_cell_length_b 3.8139
_cell_length_c 6.2631
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 90.0
